+## Adding a scenario
+
+Read-only spec (`*.readonly.spec.ts`, added to the `patient`/`clinician`
+project or its own project):
+
+- Use the saved storage state and the `arriveAt*` helpers. Only read,
+  navigate, open and cancel dialogs, and download. Never submit a form that
+  saves.
+- Tolerate both legitimate fixture states (for example, zero or more sessions,
+  or protocol assigned or unavailable) instead of assuming data. Skip with a
+  reason when a precondition such as "pair is linked" is absent.
+- If a spec intentionally triggers a denial (such as a rules probe), record
+  the outcome as data instead of letting a console error fail the run.
+
+Stateful spec (`*.stateful.spec.ts`):
+
+1. Use the `stateful` fixture and put `scope.runMarker` in a free-text field
+   of every document the UI creates.
+2. If the flow writes a collection or field that `cleanupPlan.ts` does not
+   attribute yet, add the delete rule or `restorableFields` entry first, with
+   positive and negative cases in `e2e/harness/cleanupPlan.test.ts`. Run
+   `npm run test:e2e:harness`.
+3. After every UI save, assert the stored document with an Admin helper in
+   `persistenceAssertions.ts`, not only the re-rendered UI.
+4. Run the relevant npm script in `plan` mode, review the printed plan (paths,
+   field names, reasons), and only then `execute` with its digest.
+
